      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41b4881b_208d1a13",
        "filename": "fs/crypto/keysetup.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 185,
      "author": {
        "id": 1619522
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-14T01:56:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently the wrapped master key is a key derivation key and can derive a contents encryption key for a specific block mode. In the vops we use the crypto_mode to derive the specific key for that particular crypto_mode. But not sure if all hardware would do that, so it does make sense to add this restriction.\n\nBut shouldn\u0027t we use the wrapped key only when the policy requests it rather than for the first mode that calls this function after a wrapped key is set ?",
      "parentUuid": "6b7c9820_3597c7b5",
